INT. TAXIDERMIST'S WORKSHOP - NIGHT

A long room of glass eyes. Foxes, owls, a stag with one antler snapped. Moonlight crawls over the benches. A power cut has stopped the wall clock at 2:14.

Five people stand in the dark with a single torch: BASTIAN VOLKERS, forties, who owns the place; his sister SOLENE, thirties; their cousin MERIEL, twenties; the neighbour ROYSTON, sixties; and a GIRL, perhaps ten, in a nightgown, whom no one has invited.

BASTIAN
Who let you in?

The Girl says nothing. She stares at the stag.

SOLENE
Bas, she's soaked. Look at her feet.

MERIEL
Where are your parents, sweetheart?

The Girl lifts a hand and points. Not at any of them. At the stag. Her fingers tremble.

ROYSTON
(low)
Child, that's a dead deer.

GIRL
He said I could sleep in him.

They freeze. The torch jerks. Light skates across the glass eyes, and every one seems to turn.

BASTIAN
Who said?

GIRL
(whispering)
My name is Pia.

Behind her, the stag's head slowly lowers.

PIA
(smiling)
He's very warm.
